  software to improve processing time and  power  the data sets that are analyzed are  usually very large and they take immense  amounts of computing power and memory  that many personal computers do not have  also despite being publicly available  data are also usually complex to access  and coding knowledge is usually required  to do so  similarly analysis pipelines and  programs require coding knowledge that  many biologists do not have  in a university setting students have  the opportunity to learn the  bioinformatics project  of designing and implementing a project  but do not receive practical or hands-on  experience with the full workflow  due to the faces due to the limitations  that i just mentioned  similarly faculty faces challenges with  being able to cover a diverse range of  topics if they are specialized in a  certain area of bioinformatics or if  they are unfamiliar with bioinformatics  in general for example a professor whose  research focuses on oncogene expression  might not know much about the  metagenomics of seawater  to overcome these challenges the  omixlogic portal was developed this  program aims to standardize organize and  systemize bioinformatics training in  order to make these analysis usable for  any biologist or clinician  there are some traditional problems with  the standardization of bioinformatics  coursework  which includes materials for courses  that are usually developed in-house  taught sporadically and are rarely  updated  the omixlogic portal introduces new  material that keeps up with new  technology these courses  need to be organized because the  challenge is to combine several  different topics together the flow and  transitions between subject needs to be  developed this is addressed at omics  logic through introductory material  which is being woven throughout the  courses  the last challenge we face is  systematization  how can you know that someone is stuck  and needs help or allow someone to run  forward to address this omixlogic uses  standardized modules and interactive  sessions beginning with mastering  terminology and concepts to implementing  these concepts with real data sets in a  project based approach  here is an overview of the learning  process in order to create a path of  skill development comics logic employs  the bloom's taxonomy levels of learning  this approach starts with the basics  where students recalls facts and  terminologies and are able to repeat and  memorize the material with this base the  learning builds to conceptual knowledge  being able to understand concepts and  apply information to new situations  the students will then be able to  analyze data by drawing connections and  evaluate when to use certain methods  this leads them to the highest level of  learning the ability to design and  create original work  so how do omixologic resources help  advance bioinformatics teaching  omixlogic is a portal for practical and  theoretical learning of bioinformatics  composed of courses designed to take you  through the theoretical knowledge comics  logic takes a combination of training  modules data analysis tools curated  project data sets and interactive  sessions with mentors to give a student  a clear part of the bloom's taxonomy  pyramid  no matter what the user's initial  experience with bioinformatics is comics  logic is a useful tool for gaining a  baseline knowledge of the theory behind  bioinformatics analysis of large data  sets an introduction to basic boring  languages like art and python are  beginning a data analysis project  these six courses were taken from the  core or mixed logic curriculum which is  available online  beginning with an introduction to  application of bioinformatics and an  overview of data types the student is  able to learn terminology and factual  knowledge to build upon  from there genomics translatorics  metagenomics epigenomics and data  science are introduced each course  starts with important terms and concepts  and then introduces case studies and  pipelines related to each one  this allows the students to gain the  conceptual knowledge in order to begin  their own projects  omixlogic expands upon its basic  curriculum with specialization track  projects  bioinformatics methods are best learned  in the context of real case studies  prepared by our network of mentors and  collaborators that illustrate how  various bioinformatics methods and omix  data types are used in current research  in medicine biotechnology agriculture  and even astrobiology  the projects are prepared by taking  publicly available datasets and using  them to explore and understand both the  research challenge and the analysis fact  to extract meaningful insights from  complex pharmics data  in this symposium we will hear from  speakers from different domains of life  sciences  talking about relevance of omics  integration of omix technologies  advancements in biomedical research and  also we'll hear about machine learning  view of multi-omics integration  what we will discuss today and  throughout is a result of hard work by  amazing team led by company co-founders  dr alfred dobber who comes from a  medical background has an extensive  expertise in oncology immunology and  biochemistry of information and has been  recognized internationally for his  generous support of many research  projects and initiatives that support  data science training and applications  in medicine  dr yunet brodsky is the director of  tribal bioinformatics research center at  the university of haifa and is an expert  in bioinformatics and biostatistics  he has numerous publications in  mathematics and bioinformatics and over  uh his course of his career he has  developed multiple novel algorithmic  approaches to biomedical data analysis  under his leadership the trauber  research center started collaborations  with research teams at such universities  as the university of california san  francisco institute pasture  turin university and many others where  research labs are working on  cutting-edge research projects studying  viral and bacterial infections and  designing novel drugs and vaccines to  treat and prevent infections diseases  the rest of the team includes experts in  bioinformatics computer science and  training some of our team members will  be presenting to me as well  to give students the options for  analyzing a given data set  code dependent paths or port independent  paths these data sets and associated  publications can be used in several ways  you can learn bioinformatics without any  coding at all  for that in each project we explain the  analysis pipelines on the user-friendly  tbi info platform for big data analysis  you can also learn the scripts behind  many of the steps learning to wrangle  clean visualize and analyze data in your  own analysis  finally you can hear about the projects  and their research applications in our  mental guided programs where experts  share their experience and support  research projects developed by you  here is an example of the code  independent pipeline the pipeline  builder interface on the tbi info  platform is a color coded pipeline that  helps establish a logical connection  between the technical names of data  analysis methods and the logical steps  needed to build the full pipeline  data is put in a as an input file  and then analysis can be chosen based  off on the type of research  each analysis is separated into three  columns blue for pre-processing red for  mapping and green for quantification  each time you click a button a pop-up  will contain additional information  useful for building the pipeline  the ease of the color-coded buttons  allow programs to be run without any  coding knowledge interactive outputs  allow easy visualization of the data  several demo pipelines with real data  sets are available  for students to practice the workflow  including demos on genomic variant  calling of cancer cell lines 16 as  amplicon analysis on diet and its  analysis on the microbiome and a  pipeline for examining a phytogenetic  analysis of ebola virus  to answer your curiosity about the g  biology platform we have among us  researchers for travel bioinformatics  research center who will highlight few  areas of analysis available on the  survey dr julia pano who will talk about  analysis of bulk and single cell  transcriptomics data on the t bioinfo  platform and dr elizabeth  will talk about metagenomics data on the  tip ironfor platform  after using the t bioinfo platform to  visualize the pipelines and practice  analyzing students are then able to take  their theoretical knowledge the remember  and understand levels of blooms and  apply that in a project  the apply analyze and evaluate levels of  groups then check their comprehension  with levels and batches certificates of  completion and test  similarly faculty should be able to  assign the homicide portal to their  students with an understanding that it  will give them holistic understanding  and comprehensive knowledge of  bioinformatics beginning with bytes and  molecules and onto designing their own  question based project  omixlogic employs a hybrid approach  combining learning and research to  ensure that students are building off of  the first level of knowledge taxonomy  omics logic tracks progress with  activities like pipelines coding and  literature reviews quizzes on topics key  terms and important questions and covers  a broad range of topics like biomedical  research biotechnology and agriculture  their students are able to continue  their knowledge base with a research  assessment making sure they are able to  understand methods challenges and  results as well as being able to  comprehend primary research literature  and recreate the methodology  they should also be able to ask  questions based on data exploration this  leads to the ability of to encounter  errors in their analysis apply  theoretical knowledge of why those  errors are occurring and find a solution  bioinformatics combines life science  terms with data science skills which  allows researchers to answer life  science questions with reproducible data  analysis methods  logic is proud to collaborate with many  diverse programs across the globe we  also work with over 15 000 students at  community colleges franklin j community  college  top tier universities like georgetown  university as well as 20 universities  around the world  we are pleased to have among us  researchers from our partner  universities and institutions who will  enlighten us with their talks on  different topics relevant to any student  or researcher  from knowing about technology and soft  skills uh for industry skill sets the  missing link between academia and  industry to understanding genotypic data  personalized therapies for cancer  patients and hierarchical patient models  in this presentation i explained the  current challenges and limitations in  bioinformatics  i described how we aim to address these  challenges with the omixlogic platform  we discussed bloom's taxonomy for  learning progression and how it can be  used in bioinformatics coursework  we also explore the omixologic program  and how it utilizes bloom's taxonomy in  structuring in scores  pipelines and projects  and finally described several outcomes  of the omixlogic program  want to know how to get started the  omixlogic portal is easy and free for  anyone to register with many courses  and online mental guided training  programs in the field of omics that  includes genomics transcriptomics single  cell transcriptomics metagenomics and  epigenomics  also you will find programs in the field  of bioinformatics  structural biology infectious diseases  and precision medicine  these programs are available all around  the year and you can get started with  your specialized training anytime at  your own convenience  once you have a specialized training  then you can work on an independent  research project  again under mental guidance on different  specialization tracks which includes the  analysis of data types  you learnt in the training program these  specialization tracks include oncology  infectious diseases precision medicine  neuroscience data science for biomedical  data analysis metabolic disorders space  omics agriculture and comprehensive  training on omics data analysis  throughout the year various students and  researchers joined comics research  fellowship program and work on their  research projects to either gain new  skill sets or to complete their polished  recitation or for a publication to add  to their achievements comics research  symposium will provide a stage to such  research fellows to present their  innovative research projects  also all the research projects will get  a feedback from our panel of judges  the omics logic training has been  completed by over 24 000 participants  from 187 countries in over 500 workshops  and due to this fast growth our team is  now working with local and recent  coordinators that are helping refine the  local program logistics and leverage our  online training resources adapting them  to the needs of students and researchers  around the world  as a result we have acquired  professional certification to offer our  curriculum and support research projects  using our omics logic project based  curriculum and here are some amazing  stats from an year-long training  programs that were conducted by us  the symposium is divided in three parts  where we listen to speakers from asia  first  then africa and finally the americas  so to begin with an introduction to omix  logic asia i would like to call upon  stage dr mohit mazuma  dr mohad mazundar is an experienced  viral information with multiple  publications in peer review journals he  has been developing collaborations with  universities as a mentor and project  lead for omixology training and research  fellowship  over to you dr moha